2. KaKs_Calculator 2.0 (Beijing Institute of Genomics, Chinese Academy of Sciences)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

File: R/substitutionrate.R, the internal functions

    kaks_transl_table()   the genetic codes as 64-character strings ('!' for a stop codon), copied from the
                          array 'transl_table' of src/base.cpp of KaKs_Calculator 2.0 (the codes themselves are
                          the NCBI genetic codes);
    kaks_lwl_tables()     a translation into R of the counting of sites and of transitions / transversions per
    kaks_lwl_counts()     0-, 2- and 4-fold degenerate class of src/LWL85.cpp (LWL85::CountSiteAndDiff(),
                          getCodonClass(), TransitionTransversion(), MLWL85::TransitionTransversion()) and
                          src/LPB93.cpp (MLPB93::TransitionTransversion()) of KaKs_Calculator 2.0, written so
                          that the counts are those of KaKs_Calculator to the last bit (they decide whether a
                          value that KaKs_Calculator printed is a saturated estimate).

    KaKs_Calculator 2.0: Copyright (C) 2009 Beijing Institute of Genomics of CAS. Authors: Da-Peng Wang,
    Yu-Bin Zhang (2.0), Zhang Zhang (1.0); modified version 2.0.1 by Kristian K. Ullrich (2020).
    Wang D, Zhang Y, Zhang Z, Zhu J, Yu J (2010) KaKs_Calculator 2.0: a toolkit incorporating gamma-series
    methods and sliding window strategies. Genomics Proteomics Bioinformatics 8:77-80.
    Source compared: https://github.com/kullrich/kakscalculator2 (commit 4b96206f67c934792a6d02fb38bb356056ad84f9),
    the fork of https://sourceforge.net/projects/kakscalculator2 that bioconda builds (kakscalculator2 2.0.1).
    Licence: GNU General Public License version 3 (the LICENSE file of that repository; the source files
    themselves carry only the copyright line and no "or any later version" statement).

    orthologr otherwise only runs the program KaKs_Calculator when it is installed and reads its output.


